 {"id":"CF-078","title":"P3 — node.json omits two identity fields specs/NODE.md requires, takes bus.base from an env var no layer sets, and no shipped adapter can reach the write path that would expose it","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Spec vs writer, measured at code-factory@ac30ceb (2026-11-03). specs/NODE.md:7-16 requires the manifest to carry bus.agent_id and harness.version. scripts/project-node.sh:255-266 writes bus{base} and harness{name,port} only — bus.agent_id and harness.version are absent, so a scheduler target that names the crier agent id (specs/NODE.md:19) has nothing to read. The two values it does write are not measurements: repo.path is built as '/home/'+$USER+'/repo' instead of the path the run actually used, and bus.base is read from CRIER_BASE, which grep -rn CRIER_BASE over *.sh/*.md/*.py returns exactly one hit — that same line — while layer 00 (scripts/project-node.sh:147-160) measures CRIER_URL. A run with CRIER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8799 would therefore record http://crier.example:8767. Nobody sees this because the write path is unreachable with the shipped adapters: on this host hermes --apply fails 'FAIL python — hermes-agent 0.19.0 requires python >=3.11,<3.14; found 3.14.9', opencode --check PASSes but --apply prints 'FAIL apply — refused — the opencode install ladder is unmeasured here', claude-code is 'FAIL binary — absent'; and tests/selftest.sh only ever runs scoped, where layer 90 prints 'SKIP layer 90 (fixture mode: no manifest)'. So no shipped path and no test ever produces node.json, and the one code path that does is a string-built identity record. ch:trace row=CF-078 spec=specs/NODE.md#manifest wave=none:qa-tick-no-manifest test=tests/selftest.sh doc=scripts/project-node.sh prompt=prompts/qa.md evidence=none:row-is-the-evidence witness=none:no-live-node verdict=none:filed-not-judged commit=none memory=none:no-durable-record","acceptance_criteria":"1. A green unscoped --apply writes node.json in which bus.agent_id equals the agent id in $HOME/.node/crier.json, harness.version equals the version the adapter's --check printed, repo.path equals `git -C \"$HOME/repo\" rev-parse --show-toplevel`, and bus.base equals the CRIER_URL the layer-00 reach check measured; no field may be string-concatenated or read from a variable no layer sets. 2. `grep -rn CRIER_BASE` returns zero hits, or a specs/NODE.md line that defines it as the manifest field source and a layer that measures it. 3. A committed transcript (tests/selftest.sh section or docs/audits/) shows the node.json produced by a green run, so the write path is exercised by the gate rather than by inspection. 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z"}
 {"id":"CF-079","title":"P4 — specs/NODE.md layer table names two capabilities no shipped code establishes: layer 30 'a pull worker' and layer 90 'one round trip whose digest is recomputed on the control host'","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":1,"reasoning":"Contradiction between the design authority and the script, measured at code-factory@ac30ceb. specs/NODE.md:29 says layer 30 establishes 'a crier identity file (600) and a pull worker'; scripts/project-node.sh:197-208 tests only -f $STATE/crier.json and its mode 600 — no worker, no pull, no polling process is started or checked. specs/NODE.md:31 says layer 90 establishes 'one round trip whose digest is recomputed on the control host'; scripts/project-node.sh:250-270 writes node.json and nothing else — a run prints '[90] manifest' and 'manifest is written only when every layer passes', never a digest row. CF-004 owns building the round trip (pending), and CF-068 owns the file-existence weakness of layer 30, but no row owns the spec claiming both as shipped layer behaviour, so AGENTS.md rule 1 ('a script that contradicts specs/ is a bug in one of them') has no owner. ch:trace row=CF-079 spec=specs/NODE.md#layers wave=none:qa-tick-no-manifest test=tests/selftest.sh doc=specs/NODE.md prompt=prompts/qa.md evidence=none:row-is-the-evidence witness=none:no-live-node verdict=none:filed-not-judged commit=none memory=none:no-durable-record","acceptance_criteria":"1. Every 'Establishes' cell in the specs/NODE.md layer table names only something the shipped script measures, or the script prints a row for it: layer 90 either recomputes and prints an artifact digest, or the table says it writes the node manifest and the round trip is described as CF-004 work rather than shipped behaviour. 2. `grep -n 'pull worker' specs/NODE.md` returns nothing, or `grep -n` finds the code that starts and checks a pull worker. 3. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z"}
 {"id":"CF-080","title":"P4 — --apply clones the workspace after the bus layer FAILED, manufacturing the repo-with-no-bus node AGENTS.md rule 9 forbids; only disk admission actually refuses to continue","status":"pending","priority":"P4","complexity":2,"reasoning":"Measured at code-factory@ac30ceb (2026-11-03, temp HOME, transcript reproduced in this tick): CRIER_URL=http://crier.example:8767 HOME=<tmp> ./scripts/project-node.sh --apply --project myproject --repo https://github.com/github/gitignore --ref main printed 'FAIL crier_identity — absent — stage a bundle and re-run; a node without an identity is invisible' at layer 30, then '[40] repo  ..  cloning https://github.com/github/gitignore @ main' and 'PASS repo_clone — <tmp>/repo @ 6bb5af7', ending 'NODE: FAIL (3)'. $HOME/repo existed after the run. The script's own comment at scripts/project-node.sh:141-143 says 'apply refuses immediately; check keeps measuring the other layers so one run reports every reason the node is unusable (CF-102)', but the only apply-mode refusal in the file is the disk-admission guard (require_disk). AGENTS.md rule 9 states 'Bus before workspace. A node that can receive a command but has no repo is diagnosable; a node with a repo and no bus is invisible' — a single documented --apply run produces exactly the invisible node, and a second run then reports the workspace as present, so the invisible state is durable. ch:trace row=CF-080 spec=AGENTS.md#rules wave=none:qa-tick-no-manifest test=tests/selftest.sh doc=scripts/project-node.sh prompt=prompts/qa.md evidence=none:row-is-the-evidence witness=none:no-live-node verdict=none:filed-not-judged commit=none memory=none:no-durable-record","acceptance_criteria":"1. --apply with no $HOME/.node/crier.json does not create $HOME/repo: the run stops before layer 40 and says which layer refused, proven by a tests/selftest.sh fixture that runs the real script in apply mode and asserts rc!=0 and [ ! -d \"$HOME/repo\" ]. 2. The comment at scripts/project-node.sh:141-143 is true for every layer that can fail, or it names the single layer it covers. 3. --check behaviour is unchanged: the same fixture in check mode still prints the layer-40 row (so the measurement value of a check run is preserved). 4. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS.","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:42:22Z"}
+{"id":"CF-081","title":"P3 — docs/BOARD.md 'Current measured state' is hand-typed: 61 rows/66 events/17 warnings claimed, 66/72/19 measured at 7cf19b0","status":"pending","priority":"P3","complexity":3,"reasoning":"Measured at 7cf19b0 (code-factory-readme's close of CF-065) in a clean canonical checkout, review tick code-factory-review-2026-11-03-15-39-07: docs/BOARD.md:43 says \"61 task rows, 66 events, RESULT: OK (17 warning(s))\" and line 46 says \"PASS 61/61 rows parse\"; the same tree carries 66 task rows and 72 events, boardctl prints \"RESULT: OK (19 warning(s))\", and selftest prints \"PASS 66/66 rows parse\". The block is headed \"Current measured state\" and is pinned by hand to d4eec41.\n\nNot a one-off slip — the block has been hand-corrected twice today and drifted both times: a5e7754 set it to 60 rows/64 events at e21f2ce, 91f3a64 corrected it to 61/66 at d4eec41, and it was stale again within four commits (199e5dd filed CF-076, 4b5daa3 filed CF-077, 7bcfab0/7cf19b0 filed and closed with CF-078..CF-080 plus README work — none touched the block). Nothing in the gate derives or compares these counters: tests/selftest.sh's board arm counts rows-parse and prints the live number, and no arm reads docs/BOARD.md. The disclaimer \"Re-run both commands before quoting these numbers\" documents the drift instead of preventing it; a stranger quoting the block gets numbers that are wrong by 5 rows and 6 events, the same class CF-013/CF-033/CF-054 closed for the README status table.\n\nThe repair is a guard, not another number: derive rows and events from the board in a committed check, compare against the block, and fail naming the block and both values — with a red arm proving a deliberately wrong count fails.","acceptance_criteria":"1. Reproduce at the current tip, from the repository root: the row's probe prints the doc's pair different from the measured pair and then the literal line \"DRIFT: docs/BOARD.md measured-state block is stale\" (at 7cf19b0: doc=61 66, measured=66 72, warnings=19).\n2. A committed check (a script plus a tests/selftest.sh arm, or an arm inside scripts/boardctl validate) derives the task-row and event counts from .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl and events.jsonl and exits nonzero when docs/BOARD.md's \"Current measured state\" block disagrees with them, printing a FAIL row that names the block and both numbers.\n3. Red arm proven and kept in the gate: with the block deliberately set to a wrong count (e.g. 61 while the board carries 66) the check exits nonzero and names the mismatch; with the block correct it prints PASS. Both outputs are recorded in an evidence artifact in the tree.\n4. The warning count and the \"PASS n/n rows parse\" number in the same block are either derived at check time or removed — no hand-typed counter survives that the check does not compare.\n5. bash tests/selftest.sh prints SELFTEST: PASS with no FAIL rows and keeps its existing PASS rows plus the new arm; bash scripts/boardctl validate prints RESULT: OK.\n6. The commit carries a ch:trace marker naming row CF-081, the selftest arm and the evidence artifact, and its message states AGENTS.md rule 2 (every check must be able to fail).","created_at":"2026-11-03T15:49:59Z","updated_at":"2026-11-03T15:49:59Z","detail":{"fingerprint":"cfd23f70d236ec261a59e3ebef03903190599d8d332537e66fabb04079036223"},"probe":"d=$(sed -n 's/^- `scripts\\/boardctl validate`: \\([0-9]*\\) task rows, \\([0-9]*\\) events.*/\\1 \\2/p' docs/BOARD.md); r=$(jq -s length .coding-hermes/board/tasks.jsonl); e=$(jq -s length .coding-hermes/board/events.jsonl); w=$(bash scripts/boardctl validate 2>&1 | grep -c '^\\[warn\\]'); echo \"doc=$d measured=$r $e warnings=$w\"; [ \"$d\" = \"$r $e\" ] && echo MATCH || echo \"DRIFT: docs/BOARD.md measured-state block is stale\""}
